<title>USA: Two striking UPS workers arrested in Chicago.</title>
<headline>Two striking UPS workers arrested in Chicago.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two striking UPS workers were arrested Monday and charged with disorderly conduct at the company's facility on the south side of Chicago, police said.</p>
<p>The workers were allegedly blocking early morning truck traffic into and out of the facility, a central terminal for UPS.</p>
<p>Pickets went up across the country around midnight after talks between the Teamsters union representing about 190,000 workers and the nation's largest private shipper broke down.</p>
</text>
